data.content:
Yes — use `Assert.IsInstanceOfType<T>()`, which checks the type and returns the typed instance (MSTest 3.x+):

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void Create_ReturnsCorrectHandler()
{
    var factory = new HandlerFactory();
    var result = factory.Create("email");

    var handler = Assert.IsInstanceOfType<EmailHandler>(result);
    Assert.AreEqual("email", handler.Type);
}
```

This fails with a clear message if `result` isn't an `EmailHandler`, and eliminates the hard cast + null check.
